# PART 4 — DYNAMIC AND FIXED ELEMENTS SYSTEM

This feature is mandatory.

Whenever a user creates a new template, they must decide which elements are dynamic and which are fixed.

Every supported template element must have an editable data behavior setting.

## A. Dynamic Elements

Dynamic elements can receive new values from bulk data.

Examples:

- Main heading.
- Subtitle.
- Description.
- Question.
- Answers.
- Numbers.
- Images.
- Background images.
- Background videos.
- Audio files.
- Other supported media.
- Custom text fields.

## B. Fixed Elements

Fixed elements remain identical across every generated video.

Examples:

- Logo.
- Brand watermark.
- Decorative shapes.
- Fixed headings.
- Background music.
- Fixed animations.
- Static design elements.

## C. Element-Level Controls

For every element, provide:

- Dynamic / Fixed selector.
- Variable mapping.
- Default value.
- Missing-data behavior.
- Formatting settings.
- Preview.
- Locking.
- Visibility controls.

## D. Important Rules

1. Bulk generation must replace only selected dynamic elements.
2. Fixed elements must remain unchanged.
3. Dynamic elements must retain their original formatting.
4. Text positions must not change unexpectedly.
5. Animations and transitions must remain intact.
6. Every generated video must be an independent project copy.
7. The original template must never be overwritten.
8. Users must be able to change element behavior later.

